&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;YipitData is the leading market research and analytics firm for the disruptive economy and most recently raised $475M from The Carlyle Group at a valuation of over $1B. Every day, our proprietary technology analyzes billions of alternative data points to uncover actionable insights across sectors like software, AI, cloud, e-commerce, ridesharing, and payments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our data and research teams transform raw data into strategic intelligence, delivering accurate, timely, and deeply contextualized analysis that our customers—ranging from the world’s top investment funds to Fortune 500 companies—depend on to drive high-stakes decisions. From sourcing and licensing novel datasets to rigorous analysis and expert narrative framing, our teams ensure clients get not just data, but clarity and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate globally with offices in the US, APAC, and India. Our award-winning, people-centric culture—recognized by &lt;em&gt;Inc.&lt;/em&gt; as a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.inc.com/profile/yipitdata&quot;&gt;Best Workplace&lt;/a&gt; for three consecutive years—emphasizes transparency, ownership, and continuous mastery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What It’s Like to Work at YipitData:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;YipitData isn’t a place for coasting—it’s a launchpad for ambitious, impact-driven professionals.&amp;nbsp;From day one, you’ll take the lead on meaningful work, accelerate your growth, and gain exposure that shapes careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why Top Talent Chooses YipitData:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership That Matters&lt;/strong&gt;: You’ll lead high-impact projects with real business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rapid Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: We compress years of learning into months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Merit Over Titles&lt;/strong&gt;: Trust and responsibility are earned through execution, not tenure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Velocity with Purpose: &lt;/strong&gt;We move fast, support each other, and aim high—always with purpose and intention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your ambition is matched by your work ethic—and you&#39;re hungry for a place where growth, impact, and ownership are the norm—YipitData might be the opportunity you’ve been waiting for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an Associate SEO and AEO Manager to build the foundation of YipitData’s discoverability and organic growth engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Buyers increasingly find answers through search engines and AI assistants before they ever talk to a vendor. YipitData sits on a limitless engine of proprietary insight, and this role is about pointing that engine at the market so prospects find us on their own, engage with our content, and raise their hands to talk to us. You’ll own our SEO and AEO strategy for the YipitData organization end to end: mapping the questions our buyers ask across their journey, turning that map into a content roadmap designed to be the definitive answer, and building the systems that track whether it’s working. You’ll partner closely with the YipitAgent team to produce and verify content at scale, and with marketing, product, and sales to connect organic traffic to pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder’s role. You’ll bring bleeding-edge, AI-informed tactics to a program you get to shape from the ground up, with the data, tooling, and support to move quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-branded organic sessions and AI-sourced sessions grow quarter over quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;YipitData is cited as a source in AI-generated answers for the questions our buyers ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content ships at a consistent, measurable velocity and gets refreshed when performance slips.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organic becomes a reliable, attributable source of conversions and pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote-friendly opportunity that can sit in NYC (where our headquarters is located), one of our office hubs, or anywhere else in the US.&lt;/strong&gt; However, depending upon where the remote work is performed, income could be subject to New York State tax withholding.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As Our Associate SEO and AEO Manager You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own YipitData’s overall SEO and AEO strategy, from technical foundations and on-page optimization to how our content gets surfaced and cited in AI answer engines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own keyword, query, and question mapping across the full buyer journey, identifying where prospects are searching, what they’re asking, and where we can be the definitive answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate that mapping into a prioritized content roadmap and detailed article briefs, including structure, target queries, entities, and the proof points that make a piece authoritative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the YipitAgent team on content production, and own verification and quality review of content before it goes live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain our tracking and reporting system for content velocity, non-branded organic sessions, AI-sourced sessions and visibility, AI answer citation share, organic conversion rate, and organic-sourced pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously iterate on content performance, including a disciplined refresh program that updates, consolidates, or retires pages based on data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage our third-party presence on platforms that influence both human buyers and AI models, such as Reddit, Quora, Crunchbase, G2, and industry directories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with PR on our citation strategy so our proprietary data becomes the source that publishers, analysts, and AI systems reference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement structured data, schema, internal linking, and technical SEO best practices in partnership with web and engineering stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a steady cadence of experiments on titles, formats, structure, and distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are Likely To Succeed If:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;4+ years of hands-on experience&lt;/strong&gt; in SEO, content marketing, or organic growth, ideally at a B2B SaaS or data company, and have owned measurable outcomes like organic traffic, rankings, or organic-sourced pipeline. Direct experience with AEO, generative engine optimization, or AI search visibility is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re fluent in the modern SEO toolkit and are actively experimenting with AI visibility and citation tracking tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in questions and answers, not just keywords, and can build a buyer-journey map that connects what people ask to what we should publish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write clear, specific content briefs and have a sharp editorial eye for what makes a piece genuinely authoritative versus merely optimized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing is in YipitData’s DNA. You’d rather run a scrappy experiment this week than debate the perfect plan for a month. You treat failed tests as data and you’re always exploring new tools, channels, and ideas to see what they can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable with technical SEO fundamentals, including crawlability, indexation, site structure, Core Web Vitals, and structured data, and can work effectively with engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an operator who likes building systems and processes from scratch, and you stay current on how search engines and LLMs are changing the way content gets discovered and cited.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You collaborate well across content, product, design, and sales, and communicate priorities, results, and tradeoffs clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our compensation package includes comprehensive benefits, perks, and a competitive salary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We care about your personal life, and we mean it. We offer flexible work hours, flexible vacation, a generous 401K match, parental leave, team events, wellness budget, learning reimbursement, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your growth at YipitData is determined by the impact that you are making, not by tenure, unnecessary facetime, or office politics. Everyone at YipitData is empowered to learn, self-improve, and master their skills in an environment focused on ownership, respect, and trust. See more on our high-impact, high-opportunity work environment above!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Only: &lt;/strong&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is anticipated to be &lt;strong&gt;$108K-123K&lt;/strong&gt;. Final compensation may be determined by a number of factors, including, but not limited to, the applicant’s experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, and internal team benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The compensation package also includes equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may be performed fully remotely within the United States. Please note that our US headquarters are located in NYC. If the remote work is performed outside of these offices, income may be subject to New York State tax withholding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, or veteran status. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.yipitdata.com/careers/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: #ffffff;&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;img height=&quot;1&quot; width=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;display:none;&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;https://px.ads.linkedin.com/collect/?pid=4341228&amp;amp;conversionId=10486642&amp;amp;fmt=gif&quot; /&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Corporate Marketing owns how A-LIGN is seen, heard, and trusted, leading corporate communications, brand marketing, and the creative design function, translating company strategy into a differentiated presence in the market. In this role, you will be responsible for the strategic direction and day-to-day execution of corporate communications, brand marketing, and creative across every channel A-LIGN goes to market through. As the Senior Director, Corporate Marketing, you will build and lead a multidisciplinary team spanning design and communications, while managing public relations (PR) agency and freelance partners to extend capacity. A-LIGN will depend on you to define brand architecture and messaging standards, govern visual and verbal identity globally, elevate corporate and executive thought leadership, and use artificial intelligence (AI) and self-service tools to scale creative delivery. This role partners closely with Demand Generation, Product Marketing, Sales, Partnerships, People Operations, and executive leadership to ensure corporate marketing investment tracks to business outcomes. The ideal candidate is a senior marketing leader with brand and communications depth who pairs genuine craft standards with commercial accountability, builds durable process, and thrives in a fast-paced, results-oriented environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Vice President, Marketing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Classification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-Time, Exempt&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BRAND MARKETING &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own A-LIGN’s global brand strategy (architecture, corporate positioning, messaging framework, and verbal identity) and govern its consistent application across every market-facing channel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain the messaging hierarchy that connects the corporate narrative to service line, industry, and persona-level messaging so every go-to-market team works from a single source of truth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing, which owns content strategy and production, to ensure content reflects corporate positioning, messaging, and brand standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and lead brand marketing campaigns that build awareness, authority, and reputation, partnering with Demand Generation and Product Marketing so brand investment amplifies pipeline programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own brand health measurement, including awareness, share of voice, brand sentiment, reputation, and message resonance, and present performance and recommendations to executive leadership on a regular cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ongoing research into industry trends, customer insights, and the competitive landscape to identify white space and keep A-LIGN’s voice ahead of a crowded compliance market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect the A-LIGN brand by governing trademark and logo use, partner and co-branding standards, and the accuracy and compliance of public claims, in partnership with Legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CORPORATE COMMUNICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the external communications strategy, including press releases, media relations, and announcement planning for certification, product, partnership, and corporate milestones, directing the PR agency to earn coverage that builds authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run the LinkedIn and social program across the corporate channel and executive and practitioner voices, setting the editorial approach, publishing cadence, and engagement standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the corporate and executive thought leadership program, working with internal subject matter experts and the global go-to-market function to define areas of focus and convert practitioner expertise into differentiated market commentary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run the awards and speaking program: identify high-value awards, conferences, and industry events, and prepare and submit nominations and speaking proposals that position A-LIGN leaders and practitioners as industry authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with executive leadership to build executive visibility, including media and speaking preparation, bylines, and executive social presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amplify external news, brand messaging, and company milestones to employees through internal channels, and support executive leadership on company-wide announcements in partnership with People Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the final review on external-facing communications, holding accuracy, tone, and message alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Partnerships, and People Operations to extend brand messaging into customer, partner, and employer brand communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own crisis and reputation management, including the issues and crisis communications playbook, reputation monitoring, and spokesperson readiness, and lead the cross-functional response with Legal, Security, and executive leadership when an issue could affect A-LIGN’s credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CREATIVE&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the creative function end to end, setting the standard for design and campaign creative while building the briefing structure, review cadence, and production process that allow the team to deliver at speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and lead the creative design team, and manage agency, freelance, and production partners to extend capacity without diluting quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own brand guidelines, visual identity, and templates, and govern their consistent application across the company, including video, web, and event content produced by other teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize creative delivery with AI by evaluating and adopting AI-enabled design and workflow tools and setting guardrails that protect brand quality, accuracy, and intellectual property&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build self-service creative capabilities, including templates, brand asset libraries, and intake workflows, so teams across the company can fulfill routine creative requests without creating a bottleneck for the creative team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain tight working alignment with the Product Marketing content team on video and multimedia production, setting shared briefs, brand standards, and review processes so content is on brand and delivered at speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Demand Generation and Product Marketing to integrate creative into program planning from the outset, ensuring brand and messaging directly strengthen campaign performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEADERSHIP &amp;amp; OPERATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, develop, and lead the corporate marketing team across communications, brand, and creative, defining the structure, hiring plan, and goals as the function scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the annual corporate marketing plan, priorities, and key performance indicators (KPIs) in step with the company go-to-market strategy, and report results to the Senior Vice President, Marketing, and executive leadership on a regular cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and manage the corporate marketing budget, allocating investment across communications, brand, and creative programs and across in-house and external resources, including the PR agency and freelance partners, and hold the team accountable to output and outcome targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead corporate messaging and communications planning for major company moments, such as acquisitions, leadership changes, new service launches, and rebrands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EDUCATION&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, Design, Business, or other relevant field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EXPERIENCE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of corporate marketing, communications, brand, or creative experience, including 4+ years leading and developing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and executing brand and communications strategies that delivered measurable business results in a B2B environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading corporate communications, brand, and creative functions, including direct management of designers and communications professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external agencies, freelancers, and production partners against scope, budget, and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading executive visibility, media relations, and crisis or issues communications, including working directly with C-suite leaders and PR agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience adopting AI tools and self-service workflows to improve creative or communications productivity while protecting brand quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with social media, media monitoring, and creative production tools, and reporting platforms used to measure brand, reputation, and communications performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to the cybersecurity, compliance, or professional services industry is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SKILLS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and editing ability, with the judgment to set editorial standards for others and raise the quality of work you did not create yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative point of view; you can direct design and brand creative work, give specific and actionable feedback, and defend a creative decision with clear reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable translating brand, communications, and reputation activity into commercial metrics; you can build a performance dashboard and present it to an executive audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized operator who builds structure around creative and communications work: briefs, calendars, review cycles, and clear ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and composure under pressure, with the executive presence to advise senior leaders on reputation-sensitive decisions and communicate with credibility in high-stakes moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective cross-functional collaborator with a track record of working well with Demand Generation, Product Marketing, Sales, Partnerships, Legal, and People Operations to launch integrated programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and comfortable operating in a fast-moving environment where priorities shift and agility is valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, with a drive to continuously raise the quality and impact of your team&#39;s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare, Dental, and Vision Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer Paid Life Insurance and Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EAP - Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Plan with Employer Matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Bonus Structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personalized Career Coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Office Closure December 25-January 1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vacation Bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer Hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About A-LIGN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A-LIGN is the leading provider of high-quality, efficient cybersecurity compliance programs. Combining experienced auditors and audit management technology, A-LIGN provides the widest breadth and depth of services including SOC 2, ISO 27001, HITRUST, FedRAMP, and PCI. A-LIGN is the number one issuer of SOC 2 and HITRUST and a top three FedRAMP assessor. To learn more, visit a-lign.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come Work for A-LIGN!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply online today at A-LIGN.com and learn about life at A-LIGN by following us on&lt;strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/a-lign/posts/?feedView=all&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A-LIGN is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Minorities, women, disabled, and veterans encouraged to apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(57, 116, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 24pt;&quot;&gt;About Blueprint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Blueprint is a technology solutions firm headquartered in Bellevue, Washington, with teams across the United States. We help organizations turn complex challenges into meaningful outcomes by connecting strategy and execution across AI, cloud, data, product development, and emerging technology.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Our culture is built by people who care deeply about doing exceptional work. We set high standards, take ownership, and continually challenge ourselves and one another to be better. We work hard, support each other, and take genuine pride in what we deliver for our clients, partners, and teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;At Blueprint, you’ll work alongside talented people with different experiences, expertise, and perspectives. You’ll have opportunities to take on meaningful challenges, expand your skills, and see the impact of what you build.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt; color: rgb(57, 116, 216);&quot;&gt;Bring your perspective. Raise the standard. Build what matters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work closely with marketing and business partners to plan and execute go-to-market programs for a portfolio of physical and live experiences. You will help bring a globally recognized entertainment brand to life through theme park attractions, location-based experiences, events, exhibitions, and other experiential programs. You will work with operators, venues, production companies, creative agencies, and cross-functional marketing partners to develop campaigns from strategy through execution, while managing timelines, budgets, assets, approvals, and performance reporting. The role is remote with flexibility to accommodate time-zone differences and will be measured by the successful execution of go-to-market campaigns&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;278&quot; data-end=&quot;477&quot;&gt;• Develop and activate brand marketing programs for a portfolio of theme park lands and attractions, location-based experiences, traveling exhibitions, fan events, and experiential brand activations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;479&quot; data-end=&quot;712&quot;&gt;• Partner with experience operators, production companies, venue partners, and creative agencies to develop opening campaigns, ongoing marketing programs, and seasonal campaigns that drive awareness, attendance, and brand engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;714&quot; data-end=&quot;848&quot;&gt;• Own end-to-end brand marketing for experiences, from strategy and positioning through go-to-market planning and in-market execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;850&quot; data-end=&quot;1032&quot;&gt;• Translate franchise and business priorities into clear marketing briefs, messaging frameworks, creative direction, and integrated campaigns that resonate with audiences and guests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1034&quot; data-end=&quot;1244&quot;&gt;• Build scalable frameworks, toolkits, and operating models that enable experiences marketing programs to scale across partners, venues, regions, and major franchise moments while maintaining brand consistency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1246&quot; data-end=&quot;1476&quot;&gt;• Identify opportunities to extend the brand into culture and community through fan events, conventions, pop-ups, live moments, and other experiential programs that generate earned media and reinforce broader franchise engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1478&quot; data-end=&quot;1696&quot;&gt;• Develop integrated communications plans across owned, earned, paid, partner, retail, and on-site channels, collaborating with editorial, social, web, PR, influencer, community, media, and regional marketing partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1698&quot; data-end=&quot;1847&quot;&gt;• Manage program operations including scopes, timelines, budgets, contracts, approvals, creative assets, on-site execution, invoicing, and reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1849&quot; data-end=&quot;2033&quot;&gt;• Monitor program performance, including attendance, audience growth, brand impact, and earned reach, and use insights to support continuous improvement and test-and-learn initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;2057&quot; data-end=&quot;2216&quot;&gt;• 7+ years of marketing experience in theme parks, location-based entertainment, experiential or event marketing, live entertainment, or destination marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2218&quot; data-end=&quot;2447&quot;&gt;• Direct experience working at or alongside established experience operators, IP holders, theme park organizations, location-based entertainment companies, traveling exhibitions, large-scale live events, or experiential agencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2449&quot; data-end=&quot;2609&quot;&gt;• Proven experience managing partnerships with operators, venues, production companies, and agencies while balancing brand integrity with commercial objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2611&quot; data-end=&quot;2794&quot;&gt;• Strong understanding of place-based and experiential marketing, including opening campaigns, ongoing attendance marketing, seasonal programs, and on-site guest experience marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2796&quot; data-end=&quot;2930&quot;&gt;• Experience developing and executing integrated marketing programs across owned, earned, paid, partner, retail, and on-site channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2932&quot; data-end=&quot;3096&quot;&gt;• Strong project management skills with the ability to manage multiple concurrent programs while balancing scope, timelines, budgets, venues, and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3098&quot; data-end=&quot;3225&quot;&gt;• Strong cross-functional collaboration and influencing skills within matrixed organizations and external partner environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3227&quot; data-end=&quot;3302&quot;&gt;• Strong business communication, writing, and relationship-building skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3304&quot; data-end=&quot;3422&quot;&gt;• Bachelor&#39;s degree in Marketing, Business, Communications, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;3453&quot; data-end=&quot;3603&quot;&gt;• Direct experience marketing theme park lands, attractions, location-based entertainment, or large-scale live events for IP-led experience operators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3605&quot; data-end=&quot;3756&quot;&gt;• Experience marketing global entertainment properties, gaming franchises, or other large consumer brands across both physical and digital touchpoints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3758&quot; data-end=&quot;3919&quot;&gt;• Familiarity with player- and fan-driven communities and experience creating programs that build cultural relevance, audience engagement, and repeat visitation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay ranges vary based on multiple factors including, without limitation, skill sets, education, responsibilities, experience, and geographical market. The pay range for this position reflects geographic based ranges for Washington state: &lt;strong&gt;$90,000- $100,000&lt;/strong&gt; USD annually. The salary/wage and job title for this opening will be based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience and may be outside this range.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(57, 116, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 24pt;&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Blueprint believes that healthy, supported employees do their best work. Eligible employees have access to a comprehensive benefits package that may include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Flexible Spending Account (FSA)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;401(k) retirement plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Competitive paid time off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Parental leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Professional growth and development opportunities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Benefits and eligibility may vary based on role, employment status, and location.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(57, 116, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 24pt;&quot;&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;Blueprint Technologies, LLC is an equal opportunity employer. We consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital or familial status, military or veteran status, citizenship status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(57, 116, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 24pt;&quot;&gt;Applicant Accommodations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(32, 33, 36);&quot;&gt;If you need a reasonable accommodation to participate in any part of the application or interview process, please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting@bpcs.com&quot;&gt;recruiting@bpcs.com.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;CodePath is the largest educator of college computer science students in the country. We&#39;ve trained over 40,000 students from 1,000+ universities, and our partners include Amazon, Google, and other leading technology companies. We&#39;ve spent nearly a decade training the next generation of technical talent, and we just launched a $150M initiative with Anthropic, building one of the most ambitious AI workforce programs in the world.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re now expanding into new markets and scaling our team so we can move at the speed AI is transforming the workforce. People joining CodePath now will have the opportunity to help architect the next frontier of our work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe technical skill is the fastest way to turn raw talent into real opportunity. We train the engineers the AI era runs on, building toward millions of learners, hundreds of millions in revenue, and billions in economic impact. If you want to own something and be part of a 0-to-1 journey at an organization moving at the speed of AI, this is the place to build it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote (US), with travel about once a month &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-Time &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to:&lt;/strong&gt; Head of Higher Ed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; $110,000 to $150,000 per year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;More than 50 colleges and universities offer CodePath courses for credit, taught by their own faculty or by CodePath. For a student, a seat in one of those courses means industry-vetted learning and career support built into the degree they&#39;re already earning. The courses only change outcomes if students know they exist and sign up.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;That&#39;s your job. Students find us through a professor who mentions the course before registration opens, an advisor who forwards a note, a club event, or a friend who took the course last term. Most of that reach happens through people on campus, so your work is making it easy for faculty, advisors, career services, club leaders, alumni, and Tech Fellows to carry the message for us. You&#39;ll build all of it: the toolkits and campaigns they share, the campus presence, and the student community that recruits the next cohort. You&#39;ll be measured on how many students enroll and stay through add/drop, because each filled seat is one more student getting the training we exist to provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll be a dedicated partner to our Higher Education partnerships team, who own the relationships with faculty and campus leadership, and you&#39;ll own the student side of every partner campus. Some weeks that means building a one-pager a department chair can forward on Monday, tuning an email sequence on a Wednesday, and representing CodePath at a hackathon on Friday. You&#39;ll be building this function from the ground up and you need to decide in advance how we show up and what we expect back.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner activation and campaign development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build and run a term playbook for each for-credit partner, from awareness through add/drop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Equip faculty, advisors, career services, and club leaders to market CodePath courses with toolkits, talking points, and assets they can forward&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Turn national for-credit applicants into enrolled students: find where they drop off and test what moves conversion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Run virtual info sessions and campus landing pages that end with a clear path to register&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Own email and SMS to opted-in students: build the list, run the campaigns, and work with our lifecycle contractor so campus and direct touches land as one sequence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Student community building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design how alumni, Tech Fellows, and instructors show up on campus and engage students, and build the online side of that community (Discord and similar)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Own relationships with student clubs, CS and AI organizations, hackathon organizers, and campus chapters of national organizations like ColorStack, NSBE, and SHPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Plan the event calendar a term ahead, with a clear standard for which events we do and what each should return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Tie every sign-up to a channel and a partner, test timing, message, and channel, and move time and budget to what works&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Use AI to run the playbook at 50+ campuses without adding headcount: toolkits per campus, calendars and send dates, results in one view&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like in your first year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Every partner runs a term playbook, and fill rate and melt improve at for-credit partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;National for-credit conversion is measurably higher&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Every new partner launches with a full first section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;A student advocate network is live at our largest partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The opted-in student list grows, and every sign-up traces to a channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role may be right for you if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve owned an enrollment, sign-up, or acquisition number and moved it. You set up the tracking and can show which efforts drove the result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve gotten partners to market on your behalf: individuals who carried your message because you made it easy for them, and you can show what it produced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve built a campus, ambassador, or community program from the ground up and can show what it produced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You’ve built campaigns from concept to launch, including copy and creative, and run email or SMS to a list you built, changing them based on the numbers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve decided where to spend time and money (events, channels, sponsorships) based on expected return, and cut what didn&#39;t deliver&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ve run a program across many sites at once (campuses, chapters, regions) on a fixed calendar, and kept it on schedule without a team under you&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You’ve built AI into how you work to automate the repetitive parts, and you can show what it changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You want your growth work to widen who gets into tech careers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience in enrollment or admissions marketing in higher education&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You’ve built or scaled a technical community (a student developer org, hackathon community, Discord, or dev rel program) and can show how it grew&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hands-on HubSpot experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re comfortable speaking at events and on panels on behalf of CodePath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;CodePath has standardized salaries based on the position&#39;s level, no matter where you live. For this role, we&#39;re hiring for a Senior Manager level position at an annual salary of $110,000 to $150,000. Salary is determined based on your relevant experience and skills as evaluated through our interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Time Employee Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This is a remote position—work from anywhere in the US! CodePath prioritizes employee well-being with a competitive benefits package to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness: Medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-covered for employees and dependents), employer-funded healthcare reimbursement, FSAs, and Employee Assistance Program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Financial Security: 401(k), employer-paid life &amp;amp; disability insurance, and identity theft protection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Work-Life Balance: Generous PTO, paid holidays, 10 weeks of fully paid parental leave, and an annual year-end company closure (Dec 24 – Jan 2)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Professional Growth: $1,000 annual professional development stipend and home office setup support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;​​Student Loan Forgiveness: CodePath is a qualifying employer for Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF), helping employees manage student loan debt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Additional Perks: Pet wellness plans, legal services, home/auto insurance discounts, and exclusive marketplace savings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$110,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

